<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janamejaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janamejaya was a Kuru king of the late Vedic period, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parikshit">Parikshit</a>, remembered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmanas">Brahmanas</a> as a performer of the horse sacrifice. Under him and his father the Kuru realm became the leading power of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> he is the king to whom the epic is first recited, during the great snake sacrifice he held to avenge his father's death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janamejaya.jpg" alt="Janamejaya" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_janamejaya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
